{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "094F", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Lambda$", "MATH_0003": "$K, L \\in D^-(\\mathcal{C}, \\Lambda)$", "MATH_0004": "$K$", "MATH_0005": "$L$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Lambda$", "MATH_0007": "$K \\otimes_\\Lambda^\\mathbf{L} L$", "MATH_0008": "$\\Lambda$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-locally-constant-tensor-product}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ee1b2744f8fe53f8ffa11c8aa0fec04cf85003689fb3cbd5b3269ecffcb859f2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d099daf5dfd54f7c022c28cca4f726af338e482c776961d3f5ad82b9af201e21", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a site. Let <MATH_0002> be a Noetherian ring.\nLet <MATH_0003>. If the cohomology sheaves of\n<MATH_0004> and <MATH_0005> are locally constant sheaves of <MATH_0006>-modules of\nfinite type, then the cohomology sheaves of\n<MATH_0007>\nare locally constant sheaves of <MATH_0008>-modules of finite type.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:835aac55c229f4366d616de33b649352146c6943c8a3e803140f5118334c7a5c", "unit_id": "tag:094H:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "094F", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$H^i(K \\otimes_\\Lambda^\\mathbf{L} L)$", "MATH_0002": "$H^i(\\tau_{\\geq i - 1}K \\otimes_\\Lambda^\\mathbf{L} \\tau_{\\geq i - 1}L)$", "MATH_0003": "$K$", "MATH_0004": "$L$", "MATH_0005": "$K$", "MATH_0006": "$L$", "MATH_0007": "$\\Lambda$", "MATH_0008": "$\\Lambda$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-locally-constant}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-locally-constant}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7990827cb6b4ec9e899b50dc60398a0bbc9419ebc47f2539746ad66d66b171a3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:04120cb3809fbe184920a59be60f8e00cdcb016e0dc222a079cd155309dabb94", "source_text": "We'll prove this as an application of Lemma <REF_0001>.\nNote that <MATH_0001> is the same as\n<MATH_0002>.\nThus we may assume <MATH_0003> and <MATH_0004> are bounded. By\nLemma <REF_0002>\nwe may assume that <MATH_0005> and <MATH_0006> are represented by\ncomplexes of locally constant sheaves of <MATH_0007>-modules\nof finite type. Then we can replace these complexes by\nbounded above complexes of finite free <MATH_0008>-modules.\nIn this case the result is clear.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:761fbe5a82d67ac0d0de823130ec5bd687781d72de28d67730eea05682508dcf", "unit_id": "tag:094H:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "094F", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Lambda$", "MATH_0003": "$I \\subset \\Lambda$", "MATH_0004": "$K \\in D^-(\\mathcal{C}, \\Lambda)$", "MATH_0005": "$K \\otimes_\\Lambda^\\mathbf{L} \\underline{\\Lambda/I}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Lambda/I$", "MATH_0007": "$K \\otimes_\\Lambda^\\mathbf{L} \\underline{\\Lambda/I^n}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\Lambda/I^n$", "MATH_0009": "$n \\geq 1$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-locally-constant-bounded}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:dcc8254e57a4eb96e7b0f154f7db9adc35fc15546c4e75f38a6bedd4a0211c7f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1bb88d168c23ffb66b33cd89f3cf2537b3d9b56ad5570c5dd16cd6cb2b99eb77", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a site. Let <MATH_0002> be a Noetherian ring.\nLet <MATH_0003> be an ideal.\nLet <MATH_0004>. If the cohomology sheaves of\n<MATH_0005> are locally constant\nsheaves of <MATH_0006>-modules of finite type, then the cohomology sheaves of\n<MATH_0007>\nare locally constant sheaves of <MATH_0008>-modules of finite type for all\n<MATH_0009>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:200412cdf961d2106a73630dba37181b69ac01e939df39dc68100911c5960989", "unit_id": "tag:094I:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "094F", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Lambda$", "MATH_0002": "$\\underline{\\Lambda}$", "MATH_0003": "$D(\\mathcal{C}, \\Lambda)$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Lambda$", "MATH_0005": "$D(\\mathcal{C}, \\Lambda)$", "MATH_0006": "$$\nK \\otimes_\\Lambda^\\mathbf{L} \\underline{I^n/I^{n + 1}} \\to\nK \\otimes_\\Lambda^\\mathbf{L} \\underline{\\Lambda/I^{n + 1}} \\to\nK \\otimes_\\Lambda^\\mathbf{L} \\underline{\\Lambda/I^n} \\to\nK \\otimes_\\Lambda^\\mathbf{L} \\underline{I^n/I^{n + 1}}[1]\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$$\nK \\otimes_\\Lambda^\\mathbf{L} \\underline{I^n/I^{n + 1}}\n=\n\\left(K \\otimes_\\Lambda^\\mathbf{L} \\underline{\\Lambda/I}\\right)\n\\otimes_{\\Lambda/I}^\\mathbf{L} \\underline{I^n/I^{n + 1}}\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-modules-lemma-kernel-finite-locally-constant}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{derived-lemma-cohomology-in-serre-subcategory}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-locally-constant-tensor-product}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:301806514084e3024915701e097b00cbce9a6438203a0fb9d74dcc0cdabbdb7b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:eb8ea10be3182daf51ea159016302a616d28115b401331d1caa9f181155fe55e", "source_text": "Recall that the locally constant sheaves of <MATH_0001>-modules of finite type\nform a weak Serre subcategory of all <MATH_0002>-modules, see\nModules on Sites, Lemma\n<REF_0001>.\nThus the subcategory of <MATH_0003> consisting of\ncomplexes whose cohomology sheaves are locally constant sheaves\nof <MATH_0004>-modules of finite type forms a strictly full, saturated\ntriangulated subcategory of <MATH_0005>, see\nDerived Categories, Lemma <REF_0002>.\nNext, consider the distinguished triangles\n<MATH_0006>\nand the isomorphisms\n<MATH_0007>\nCombined with Lemma <REF_0003>\nwe obtain the result.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b1804eda0831a3955ea234f71f3752139ced8a92eeb2ad2a56a67478fa2b4b21", "unit_id": "tag:094I:proof"}
